// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Lena Marsh, a US citizen and freelance data engineer, 2026-01-01 .. 2026-06-30. She bills a Dutch client in EUR and a
// British one in GBP, is paid into a Wise account, and moves from Austin to Lisbon on 02-15, with a trip to London in
// March and a week in Austin in May. She is a cash-basis sole proprietor. The book stresses what a person abroad needs:
// currencies held as parcels (FIFO, with a basis in USD), the day-count tests (FEIE, Portugal's 183 days), and the
// FBAR's peak balances.
//
// Written against PROPOSAL §6 and ASSOCIATIONS.md.   ✗ cannot say  ✎ says it badly  ? unclear  ⇄ sync  ▸ derived
// Ids: ex-c04 is expat, c = cannot say, 04; [A6] is the change in REPORT.md that closes it. Rates are the book's own
// illustration (a straight line between month starts, rounded to 4 places): not market data. Every receipt, conversion
// and balance below is a replay of the lines, with FIFO parcels per currency. The FEIE limit (132,900 USD for 2026)
// and the thresholds are from memory of the IRS notices: verify.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

base USD
use us
use us/se                 // self-employment tax (a sketch, as in freelancer.ax)
use us/feie               // a sketch: Form 2555, the exclusion and its two tests. Not in crates/systems; see the closing block
use pt                    // ? ex-u02 [open] there is no `pt` system (see the move on 02-15)

sync prices               // ⇄ ex-s06 the ECB's daily EUR and GBP rates into prices/{year}.ax; the Treasury's year-end rates arrive in January
  into prices/{year}.ax
sync wise                 // ⇄ ex-s07 Wise's statement CSV carries the rate and the fee of every conversion, so a conversion is read, not typed
  read "imports/wise-*.csv"
sync bcp                  // ⇄ ex-s07 Millennium bcp exports "dd-mm-yyyy" dates and decimal commas
  read "imports/bcp-*.csv"

entity lena : person
  born    1989-03-12
  filing  single
  citizen us              // taxed by the US wherever she lives
  lives   us/tx           // moves on 02-15. ? ex-u04 [open] which rate turns a foreign receipt into USD (the day's, or the IRS yearly average that `us` brings) is a choice of the *return*, made once and used for all: nothing holds it. This book uses the day's (`rates spot`)

/// Her business, as a taxpayer sees it: nothing but her. What it earns reaches her return on Schedule C.
entity lena-studio : sole-proprietorship
  owner lena

// ── who she works for: engagements are relators (ASSOCIATIONS.md §5); both clients are abroad ──────────

entity vondel : client    // Amsterdam. 6,500.00 EUR a month, for the month before, paid by SEPA on about the 18th
entity tern-co : client   // London. 3,200.00 GBP a month, for the month before, on about the 20th
contract vondel-retainer : engagement
  provider lena-studio
  client vondel
  6_500.00 EUR monthly on last invoiced due 18d
contract tern-retainer : engagement
  provider lena-studio
  client tern-co
  3_200.00 GBP monthly on last invoiced due 20d

// ── homes: two leases, one ended and one begun ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

entity oak-court : landlord
entity sr-ferreira : landlord       // a person, but the kind is a role: here he is the landlord
contract apartment-rent : lease
  tenant lena
  landlord oak-court
  1_850.00 USD monthly on 1 from chase/checking #rent until 2026-02-14       // notice given 01-14
  deposit 1_850.00 USD
contract pt-rent : lease
  tenant lena
  landlord sr-ferreira
  1_450.00 EUR monthly on 1 from bcp/checking #rent from 2026-03-01
  deposit 2_900.00 EUR
contract health-us with blue-shield
  540.00 USD monthly on 5 from chase/checking #premium until 2026-02-14
contract expat-health with cigna
  310.00 USD monthly on 15 from chase/checking #premium from 2026-02-15

// ── positions: by institution, the paths are the shortest that are unique ───────────────────────────────

entity chase : bank
  lena/checking : deposit
  lena/savings  : deposit
entity wise : money-transfer
  lena/main : deposit holds EUR, GBP          // ? ex-u05 [open] one account with two currency balances: for the FBAR it is one account (Wise Europe SA is Belgian)
entity bcp : bank
  lena/checking : deposit holds EUR           // a second `checking`: the paths are now lena/chase/checking and lena/bcp/checking, and `chase/checking` and `bcp/checking` suffice

entity blue-shield, cigna : health-insurer
entity irs : tax-authority
entity heb, pingo-doce : grocer
entity tap-air : airline
entity airbnb, hotel-soho : lodging
entity edp : utility
entity meo : phone-company

// ═════ 2025-12-31 ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

opening 2025-12-31
  chase/checking        21_350.40 USD
  chase/savings          8_000.00 USD
  wise                   5_200.00 EUR   basis 6_059.04 USD since 2025-12-19
  wise                   1_800.00 GBP   basis 2_410.20 USD since 2025-12-22
  oak-court owes lena 1_850.00 USD ^deposit                      // the Austin deposit
  vondel owes lena 6_500.00 EUR due 01-18 ^inv-vd-2512           // December's invoices, issued on 12-31
  tern-co owes lena 3_200.00 GBP due 01-20 ^inv-tc-2512
  // ▸ foreign accounts at 12-31: 5,200.00 EUR + 1,800.00 GBP = 8,475.40 USD at the 01-01 prices: under the FBAR's 10,000 USD threshold


2026-01

01 apartment-rent                                               // ▸ 1,850.00 USD #rent of the Austin apartment, from chase/checking

05 health-us                                                    // ▸ 540.00 USD #premium

09 chase/checking -> heb 312.55 USD #groceries

15 chase/checking -> irs 3_200.00 USD #estimated-tax for 2025   // ✎ ex-b02 [A6] the January installment belongs to the year before (fl-b06, sb-b27)
20 wise <- vondel 6_500.00 EUR ^inv-vd-2512                     // ▸ settles the 12-31 invoice, for 2025-12. Income 7,592.65 USD at 1.1681 USD/EUR, the day's price: she is cash basis, so the receipt day is the day. The new EUR parcel carries it as basis
                                                                // ✗ ex-c04 [A6] the invoice it settles is for December: that is when and where the work was done, the date FEIE reads. Her return reads the day the money came (01-20). v4 has one
                                                                //         `for`, and recognizes by it, so a cash-basis tally would put this in 2025. Two readers need two calendars: the tax tally by day received, foreign-earned by day earned.

21 wise <- tern-co 3_200.00 GBP ^inv-tc-2512                    // ▸ income 4,312.00 USD at 1.3475 USD/GBP

22 wise -> 5_000.00 EUR @ 1.1684 USD into chase/checking ^fx-0122
     - 20.50 EUR #fees via wise
                                                                // ✎ ex-b03 [A10] a conversion between two of my own positions with the fee in the source currency (sb-b22): `@` names one subject position, the other end is `into`
                                                                // ▸ FIFO relieves 5,020.50 EUR from the 2025-12-19 parcel; 5,842.00 USD arrive; gain 16.00 USD on the 5,826.00 USD of basis that left; the fee's 23.89 USD of basis is cost
                                                                // ? ex-u03 [open] §988(e) exempts a personal-transaction currency gain of 200 USD or less. She holds business receipts and spends them on rent: which kind of transaction is it? (sb-u23)

31 vondel-retainer                                              // ▸ vondel owes lena 6,500.00 EUR due 02-18 ^inv-vd-2601, for 2026-01; a claim, not income: she is cash basis
31 tern-retainer                                                // ▸ tern-co owes lena 3,200.00 GBP due 02-20 ^inv-tc-2601

31 chase/checking = 21_289.85 USD
31 wise = 6_679.50 EUR
31 wise = 5_000.00 GBP

2026-02

01 apartment-rent                                               // ▸ 925.00 USD: 14 of 28 days, the lease ends 02-14. The deposit is the landlord's claim until the unit is checked

05 health-us                                                    // ▸ 540.00 USD #premium: the last; the contract ends 02-14

10 chase/checking -> tap-air 842.00 USD #travel "AUS-LIS, one way"

15 lena now lives pt                                            // ? ex-u02 [open] no `pt` system exists: nothing knows Portuguese income tax, IRS Jovem, the 183-day rule or the NIF. `lives` takes the name and no law reads it
                                                                //         and the US-Portugal totalization agreement (which country's social security a self-employed citizen pays, by certificate of coverage) is a law of two systems at once
15 lena now in pt                                               // ? ex-u01 [A12] where she lives and where she is are two timelines. `lives` moves once, here; presence moves with every trip (03-23, 05-09). The 330-day test
                                                                //         reads presence, the 183-day rule too. ▸ presence defaults to residence: nobody writes `in` unless the two differ. 02-15 is her first full day abroad
15 wise -> airbnb 1_120.00 EUR #lodging "Alfama, 14 nights"     // ▸ 1,308.38 USD at 1.1682; basis 1,307.75 USD; gain 0.63 USD on the euros spent (§988, ordinary)
15 expat-health                                                 // ▸ 310.00 USD #premium, from today, in place of health-us

19 wise <- vondel 6_500.00 EUR ^inv-vd-2601                     // ▸ income 7,590.70 USD at 1.1678. Earned in January, in Texas: US-source, not foreign earned income
20 wise <- tern-co 3_200.00 GBP ^inv-tc-2601                    // ▸ income 4,294.08 USD at 1.3419
20 wise -> 2_400.00 GBP @ 1.1487 EUR into wise ^fx-0220
     - 12.00 GBP #fees via wise
                                                                // ✎ ex-b03 [A10] the same position at both ends: an exchange inside one account, at a cross rate (EUR per GBP) that the day's two prices already imply
                                                                // ▸ FIFO: 2,412.00 GBP leave from the 2025-12-22 parcel (1.3390 basis); 2,756.88 EUR arrive worth 3,218.93 USD at 1.1676; basis that left 3,218.78 USD; gain 0.15 USD; the fee's 16.09 USD is cost

27 wise -> bcp/checking 6_000.00 EUR                            // ▸ a transfer: parcels move with their basis and day; nothing is realized. SEPA, no fee
                                                                // ▸ basis moved 7,008.47 USD: 5,559.50 EUR from 2026-01-20, 440.50 EUR from 2026-02-19
27 bcp/checking -> sr-ferreira 2_900.00 EUR due 2027-02-28 ^pt-deposit "caucao, two months"  // ▸ a claim in euros: sr-ferreira owes lena 2,900.00 EUR, carrying the 3,387.49 USD of basis that left. Nothing realized now
                                                                // ✎ it is the lease's `deposit 2,900.00 EUR` term: this line is its payment, which a typed `lease` implies (ll-b03)

28 vondel-retainer                                              // ▸ vondel owes lena 6,500.00 EUR due 03-18 ^inv-vd-2602, for 2026-02; a claim, not income: she is cash basis
28 tern-retainer                                                // ▸ tern-co owes lena 3,200.00 GBP due 03-20 ^inv-tc-2602

28 chase/checking = 18_672.85 USD
28 wise = 8_816.38 EUR
28 wise = 5_788.00 GBP
28 bcp/checking = 3_100.00 EUR

2026-03

01 pt-rent                                                      // ▸ 1,450.00 EUR #rent from bcp/checking: 1,691.42 USD at 1.1665; basis 1,693.74 USD; loss 2.32 USD on the euros

03 chase/checking <- oak-court 1_850.00 USD ^deposit            // ▸ settles the opening claim

05 bcp/checking -> pingo-doce 168.30 EUR #groceries             // ▸ 196.49 USD · loss 0.10 USD

08 bcp/checking -> edp 62.10 EUR #utilities

12 bcp/checking -> meo 39.99 EUR #phone

15 expat-health                                                 // ▸ 310.00 USD #premium

18 wise <- vondel 6_500.00 EUR ^inv-vd-2602                     // ▸ income 7,608.90 USD at 1.1706. February: 14 days worked in Texas, 14 in Lisbon: half is foreign earned income
                                                                // ✗ ex-c04 [A6] the source is a set of days, not an interval: `total(#consulting, where lena.in is foreign)` over a flow recognized per day. v4 `total` takes DATE..DATE only

19 wise <- tern-co 3_200.00 GBP ^inv-tc-2602                    // ▸ income 4,300.16 USD at 1.3438
20 wise -> bcp/checking 3_000.00 EUR                            // ▸ a transfer; basis moves

21 wise -> 3_000.00 GBP @ 1.1473 EUR into wise ^fx-0321
     - 15.00 GBP #fees via wise
                                                                // ▸ 3,441.90 EUR arrive worth 4,031.50 USD; loss 8.62 USD

23 lena now in gb                                               // ? ex-u01 [A12] a trip: still abroad for the 330-day test, no longer in Portugal for the 183-day rule. A third value of the same timeline, which `lives` cannot hold
                                                                // ⇄ ex-s08 presence from flight bookings and the phone's location history, as `now in` statements: nobody types a travel log
23 bcp/checking -> tap-air 168.40 EUR #business-travel "LIS-LGW return"

24 wise -> hotel-soho 395.00 GBP #business-travel "three nights, tern workshop"  // ▸ 531.43 USD at 1.3454; basis 530.05 USD; gain 1.38 USD on the pounds spent. A deductible cost of lena-studio

27 lena now in pt

28 wise -> 4_000.00 EUR @ 1.1730 USD into chase/checking ^fx-0328
     - 16.40 EUR #fees via wise
                                                                // ▸ 4,692.00 USD arrive; gain 20.99 USD; FIFO from the oldest parcels first (01-20, 02-19)

31 vondel-retainer                                              // ▸ vondel owes lena 6,500.00 EUR due 04-18 ^inv-vd-2603, for 2026-03; a claim, not income: she is cash basis
31 tern-retainer                                                // ▸ tern-co owes lena 3,200.00 GBP due 04-20 ^inv-tc-2603

